> However, I'm unsure how to specify the moderators in the analysis. Would it just be a case of adding:
> M~W:M + V:M
> Y~Z:Y
>
> to the model specification? I know that you can specify a separate regression coefficient per group if your moderator is categorical (see here <https://groups.google.com/d/msg/lavaan/RW_3TMARGhY/DTngJibYM3AJ>), but I don't think that applies here as all variables are continuous.

I'm not sure whether this allows you to estimated moderated mediation in lavaan, but to use interaction terms in the lavaan syntax, you'll need to manually calculate the product term in your data.frame.  And as such, you'll need to give them appropriate names (i.e., without the colon).  For example, you could create product term for Z times Y called ZY, then include ' Y ~ ZY ' in your syntax.

Terry

