MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

    The model is statistically not identified.  lavaan estimates factor-based models, and even "formative measurement" needs the factor-based model to meet identification conditions.  In your model, LAT2 must be identified as a common factor. Standard identification rules explain that a factor is identified based on other variables being dependent on it.  In your model, nothing is dependent on LAT2.
     If you specify that the residual variance of LAT2 is 0 (LAT2~~0*LAT2) and offer starting values for paths linked to LAT2, your model might achieve identification.
 --Ed Rigdon

Sent from my iPad

